# Voice AI Service - Project Rules (Cursor)

These rules are auto-applied by Cursor to keep code and workflow consistent.

## Conventional Commits

Format: `<type>(<scope>): <description>`

Valid types: feat, fix, docs, style, refactor, perf, test, chore, ci, build, revert

Guidelines:

- Header ≤ 50 chars, imperative mood, no trailing period
- Body lines ≤ 100 chars, explain WHAT and WHY
- Optional footer: issue refs (`Closes #123`), BREAKING CHANGE

## Repository Structure

```
src/
  app/                 # Next.js App Router pages & API routes
  components/ui/       # UI primitives
  lib/                 # Utilities (e.g., iframe helpers)
```

Path alias: `@/*` → `./src/*` (see `tsconfig.json`). Always use `@/` imports.

## TypeScript & Linting

- Target: ESNext; strict mode enabled
- Run `pnpm lint` before committing
- No `console.log` in production paths; prefer proper logging
- Prefer explicit types for exported APIs; avoid `any` unless pragmatic

## Next.js (App Router)

- Client components must start with `"use client"`
- Keep server code free of browser-only APIs
- Co-locate simple route utilities in `src/lib/`

## Iframe Auth Guidelines

- Token format: `sha256(secret:nonce:timestamp)` (hex)
- Enforce timestamp skew check (±300s by default)
- Read `IFRAME_API_SECRET` from env; fail fast if missing
- In dev, restrict CORS to `NEXT_PUBLIC_ALLOWED_ORIGINS`

## Environment Variables

- `IFRAME_API_SECRET` (required in all environments)
- `NEXT_PUBLIC_ALLOWED_ORIGINS` (dev convenience list)

Never commit secrets. Use `.env.local` locally and platform secrets in prod.

## Security

- Use strong, rotated secrets
- Avoid storing sensitive data in the iframe state
- Validate all incoming query params and reject on parse errors

## CI/Quality Gates (local)

- `pnpm lint` passes
- Project builds: `pnpm build`

## Contribution Workflow

- Branch names: `feature/<subject>` or `bugfix/<subject>`
- Conventional commits only
- Keep PRs small and focused; include README updates when user-facing
